% The customs background (lpsPlus docs/strategy/FactsBackground.md §6.1):
% the words of sellers for clocks, watches and their parts, in the words of
% the tariff (Chapter 91). Each word cites the text that says what it
% means: the tariff's headings and notes, US Customs rulings, the
% encyclopedia (Wikipedia: what a quartz, a mechanical, an automatic watch
% is; what a crown, a crystal, a watch strap is), and the description of
% the listings' fields (sources/listings/marketplace_fields_other_products.txt)
% for what a field means. Bridges.
%
% What it reads: the name of a good and the fields that name its kind
% ("Item Type: Watchbands", "Type: Watches for Parts", "Category: Smart
% Watches"). The words give the kind (a wrist watch, a watch strap, a dial
% ...), and the features the subheadings read: electrically operated (a
% quartz or a digital watch), a mechanical movement, automatic winding, a
% mechanical display (hands) or an opto-electronic display (digits). The
% shop's category "Watches > Watches Accessories" says that a part is for a
% watch. The metal of a strap or a case ("Material: Stainless Steel",
% "Metals Type: Zinc Alloy") is read by the jewellery background, plastics
% ("Material: Silicone") by the materials background.
%
% Two words are claims to headings outside the model (gri.le). A smart
% watch is a data apparatus of heading 8517 (US Customs, HQ H260060); a
% watch repair kit is a set of hand tools of Chapter 82. The office answers
% the claim; the model gives such a good no code of Chapter 91.
%
% Left out, because no saved text says what the word means for the tariff:
%   - "watch box", "watch winder", "watch stand", "watch holder": a box for
%     watches is a container of heading 4202, a winder a machine; no ruling
%     is saved;
%   - "Function: Alarm Clock,...,Chronograph": the functions of a watch,
%     not its kind (a wrist watch with an alarm is no alarm clock);
%   - "kinetic", "solar", "eco-drive": the power of a watch that no saved
%     ruling names in the seller's word;
%   - "sapphire crystal", "mineral glass": a watch glass is classified by
%     its material (note 1(a)), which the word does not always say.
% "Item Type: Watch Cases" is read as the case of a watch (heading 9111), as
% the tariff uses the word; a seller may also mean a box to keep watches in.
%
% Used only to read facts from a text (language reference §14.5).

the target language is: prolog.

the functions are:
    the kind of *a good* is *a kind*.

the templates are:
    *a thing* is called *a name*; undefined.
    the field *a field* of *a thing* reads *a value*; undefined.
    *a field* is a field that names the timepiece kind.
    *a name* is a word for the timepiece kind *a kind*.
    *a name* is a word for electrically operated timepieces.
    *a name* is a word for mechanical movements.
    *a name* is a word for automatic winding.
    *a name* is a word for mechanical displays.
    *a name* is a word for opto-electronic displays.
    *a name* is a word for parts for watches.
    *a name* is a word for a claim to *a kind*.
    *a thing* is named by the word *a name*.
    the kind of *a good* is *a kind*.
    *a good* is electrically operated.
    *a good* has a mechanical movement.
    *a good* has automatic winding.
    *a good* has a mechanical display.
    *a good* has an opto-electronic display.
    *a good* is for a watch.
    *a good* is claimed to belong to *a kind*.

