% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The rules: a word in the name, or in a field that names the kind
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
rule named_by_name with provenance the other products listing format,
        confer "A listing offers one finished product for sale":
a thing is named by the word a name
    if the thing is called the name.

rule named_by_field with provenance the other products listing format,
        confer "Item Type (99 listings): the kind of product in the seller's words":
a thing is named by the word a name
    if the field a field of the thing reads the name
    and the field is a field that names the timepiece kind.

rule timepiece_kind with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "CLOCKS AND WATCHES AND PARTS THEREOF":
the kind of a good is a kind
    if the good is named by the word a name
    and the name is a word for the timepiece kind the kind.

rule timepiece_electric with provenance the Wikipedia article Quartz clock,
        confer "Quartz clocks and quartz watches are timepieces that use an electronic oscillator regulated by a quartz crystal to keep time":
a good is electrically operated
    if the good is named by the word a name
    and the name is a word for electrically operated timepieces.

rule timepiece_mechanical with provenance the Wikipedia article Mechanical watch,
        confer "A mechanical watch is a watch that uses a clockwork mechanism to measure the passage of time":
a good has a mechanical movement
    if the good is named by the word a name
    and the name is a word for mechanical movements.

rule timepiece_automatic with provenance the Wikipedia article Automatic watch,
        confer "An automatic watch, also known as a self-winding watch or simply an automatic":
a good has automatic winding
    if the good is named by the word a name
    and the name is a word for automatic winding.

rule timepiece_mechanical_display with provenance the Wikipedia article Watch,
        confer "Traditionally, watches have displayed the time in analog form":
a good has a mechanical display
    if the good is named by the word a name
    and the name is a word for mechanical displays.

rule timepiece_opto_display with provenance the Wikipedia article Watch,
        confer "A digital display shows the time as a number":
a good has an opto-electronic display
    if the good is named by the word a name
    and the name is a word for opto-electronic displays.

rule for_watches with provenance the other products listing format,
        confer "Watches > Watches Accessories":
a good is for a watch
    if the good is called a name
    and the name is a word for parts for watches.

rule timepiece_claim with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "CLOCKS AND WATCHES AND PARTS THEREOF":
a good is claimed to belong to a kind
    if the good is named by the word a name
    and the name is a word for a claim to the kind.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Tests
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

query kinds is:
    the kind of which good is which kind.

query features is:
    which good is electrically operated.

query movements is:
    which good has a mechanical movement.

query windings is:
    which good has automatic winding.

query mechanical_displays is:
    which good has a mechanical display.

query opto_displays is:
    which good has an opto-electronic display.

query claims is:
    which good is claimed to belong to which kind.

query watch_parts is:
    which good is for a watch.

scenario watches is:
    watch 1 is called "quartz wristwatches".
    watch 1 is called "analog".
    the field "item type" of watch 2 reads "digital watch".
    watch 3 is called "automatic watch".
    watch 3 is called "analog watch".
    the field "category" of watch 4 reads "smart watches".
    clock 5 is called "digital alarm clock".
    kinds expects answers ["the kind of watch 1 is wrist watch", "the kind of watch 2 is wrist watch", "the kind of watch 3 is wrist watch", "the kind of watch 4 is smart watch", "the kind of clock 5 is alarm clock"].
    features expects answers ["watch 1 is electrically operated", "watch 2 is electrically operated", "clock 5 is electrically operated"].
    movements expects answers ["watch 3 has a mechanical movement"].
    windings expects answers ["watch 3 has automatic winding"].
    mechanical_displays expects answers ["watch 1 has a mechanical display", "watch 3 has a mechanical display"].
    opto_displays expects answers ["watch 2 has an opto-electronic display", "clock 5 has an opto-electronic display"].
    claims expects answers ["watch 4 is claimed to belong to transmission apparatus of heading 8517"].

scenario accessories is:
    the field "item type" of band 1 reads "watchbands".
    the field "item type" of case 2 reads "watch cases".
    case 2 is called "watches > watches accessories".
